codemap 9
tour platform-script
kind flow
author ai
group render
note The test script runner, how a GUI scenario drives the real window with no hand on the mouse. CODEMAP_SCRIPT names a file of commands, one per line (blank lines and # comments skipped). Before each frame the loop runs lines until one produces input or waits; the input goes into the same accumulated Input a real event would write, so the app cannot tell a script from a person, and every input command is a frame of its own. The loop understands only input and timing: wait <n> lets n frames pass, pause <ms> lets wall time pass while frames keep coming, mouse, down [ctrl|shift|alt] [twice], up, wheel <dy> [ctrl|shift], key <name> [ctrl] [alt] and text <chars> are input, click, dblclick and drag expand into the lines that perform them, the -id forms aim at an element by name, and quit ends the run. Every other line is the app's own command (tab, open, idle, rect, shot, dump and so on), handed to App::script, which can ask for it to run again next frame. While a script runs, real input is ignored and each frame is 8 ms apart.

